# Expected conflict — Globex service credits (gold CONF-002)

A 99.4% month sits in the first band, where SYN-009 says 10% and SYN-010 says 20%. Both
definitions apply, neither is an exception to the other, and the interpreter says so. This
test exists to lock that behaviour in: if it ever starts returning a number, someone has
invented a precedence the documents do not contain.

> Using Conflict_service_credit_acme_globex as G

```catala
declaration scope TestGlobexConflict:
  output computation content G.GlobexServiceCredit

scope TestGlobexConflict:
  definition computation equals
    output of G.GlobexServiceCredit with {
      -- monthly_uptime: 99.4
      -- monthly_service_fee: $30,000
    }
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope TestGlobexConflict
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  During evaluation: conflict between multiple valid consequences for
│  assigning the same variable.
│
├─➤ src/conflict_service_credit_acme_globex.catala_en:39.24-27:
│    │
│ 39 │     consequence equals 10%
│    │                        ‾‾‾
├─ CONFLICT — service credits, Acme Cloud Systems / Globex Retail Group (ACME-GBX-MSA-2026)
│  └─ SYN-009 § 2.1 — Service Level Exhibit tier table
│
├─➤ src/conflict_service_credit_acme_globex.catala_en:59.24-27:
│    │
│ 59 │     consequence equals 20%
│    │                        ‾‾‾
└─ CONFLICT — service credits, Acme Cloud Systems / Globex Retail Group (ACME-GBX-MSA-2026)
   └─ SYN-010 § 2.1 — Service Level Addendum tier table
#return code 123#
```
